Z||000003||conductor||11-15-2001||04:33 PM||||thnx for the url JohnF, but what should I do now. What do I need to check first, how do I check?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR> Someone had this combination of 24 and 35 as well on their 4-banger?<BR>Thnx Richard, Amersfoort, the Netherlands.||||reg||1
Z||000004||troydeb||11-15-2001||04:37 PM||||i just found out mine had a code 35 last week.  its the idle air control.  the part costs abour $52.00.  I read that if you car idles 50 rpm higher than it should for 30 seconds it will trip the check engine light||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||11-15-2001||05:34 PM||||Your see the "Vehicle Speed Sensor" is throwing a code 24.  This should only set when the drive wheels are turning.  Check connections at the ECM and TPS (Throttle Position Sensor).  I might would even replace the TPS, if it were mine.  <P>The 35 code is related to idle set.  It is very probably a vaccuum  problem, I think.  I'd start by looking for one anyway.  Other wise the fix is supposed to be to replace the IAC (Idle Air Control) unit.<P>Go to Chapter 6 of the Haynes manual.<P>As to back-up lights, they are not related to these issues.  Just check out your switch and circuitry and power (fuse) and ground.<P>Best I can do - anyone else want to jump in?||||reg||1
